 "良": "حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good (quality, condition, etc.)]\nمثال: トマトの作柄は良だ。\n→ The tomato crop is of good quality. / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [Good (grade)]\non a 優, 良, 可 scale\nمثال: 今学期は良が２つあった。\n→ I got two Bs this semester.",
 "良い": "حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good]\nalso いい (all senses)\nمثال: 私にはよい友達が数人いる。\n→ I have several good friends. / كَافٍ (sufficient) / تَمَامًا (Sufficiently.) / مَه, كَفَى (Stop! Don't do that any more! It is too much!)  [enough] / مُفِيد (Helpful or good to something or someone.)  [beneficial] / حَسَنًا, أُوكِي (Endorsement; approval; acceptance; acquiescence.)  [OK]\nas て(も)良い, と(も)良い, etc.; indicates permission or compromise",
 "良い具合に": "بِسَعَادَة (In a happy or cheerful manner; with happiness.)  [happily]",
 "良い塩梅に": "لِحُسْن اَلْحَظّ (it is fortunate that)  [fortunately]",
 "良い時間": "مُتَأَخِّر (Near the end of a period of time.) / مُتَأَخِّر (Not arriving or occurring until after an expected time.) / مَرْحُوم (Recently deceased, dead: used particularly when speaking of the dead person's ac) / مُتَأَخِّرًا (After a deadline has passed, past a designated time.)  [(getting) late] / [good time (for doing something) ; good timing]",
 "良い気": "مُتَفَائِل (Expecting the best in all possible ways.)  [optimistic]",
 "良い目": "[dice roll with the desired result ; lucky throw of the dice] / بِالتَّوْفِيق!, حَظًّا سَعِيدًا! (Used to wish fortune on someone or as encouragement; a benediction or valedictio)  [good luck]",
 "良からぬ": "سَيِّئ, وحش (Good, superlative, excellent, cool.)  [bad]\nمثال: 彼はいつもよからぬ事を企んでいる。\n→ He is always up to no good.",
 "良き": "خَيْر (The state or characteristic of being good.) / خَيْر, صَلَاح (The good, nutritional, healthy part or content of something.)  [goodness]\nمثال: 私たちは彼をよき先輩として尊敬している。\n→ We respect him as a good senior. / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good]",
 "良く": "كَمَا يَجِب, كَمَا يَنْبَغِي (In a proper manner, appropriately, suitably; correctly, justifiably)  [properly]\nمثال: そのプロジェクトはよく計画されていて興味深いが、当面の利益には大した結果をもたらさないと見られている。\n→ The project is well-planned and interesting, but its immediate impact on the bottom line is not considered substantial. / كَثِيرًا, غَالِبًا (Frequently; many times on different occasions.)  [often]\nمثال: みつなは綺麗好きだから、よく自ら進んで掃除をしています。\n→ Mitsuna is very tidy so she often cleans up without being asked. / [I'm glad that you ... ; thank you for ...]\nمثال: ジャック、よく来てくれたね。\n→ You are welcome, Jack! / [(you have) quite the nerve to ; I don't know how you can ...]\nمثال: よく、そんな口がきけるな！\n→ How dare you say that!",
 "良くある質問": "أَسِئْلَة مُكَرَّرَة (An online document containing a list of the questions most often asked about a p)  [frequently asked questions]",
 "良くする": "حَسَّنَ (To make (something) better; to increase the value or productivity (of something)) / تَحَسَّنَ (To become better.)  [to improve]\nمثال: 仕事をよりよくする方法について考えるよりも金もうけする方法を考える方が先なのである。\n→ Figuring a way to make a dollar comes ahead of thinking about how to do the job better. / [to do often]\nمثال: これは学生がよくする間違いだ。\n→ This is a mistake students are apt to make. / [to be kind to ; to treat well]\nمثال: 母は植木の世話をよくする人だ。\n→ My mother looks after the plants well.",
 "良くできました": "أَحْسَنْتَ, أَحْسَنْتِ (An exclamation of praise or endorsement of an achievement.)  [well done]\noft. stamped onto homework assignments etc. as the equiv. of a gold or silver star sticker",
 "良くないね": "[(that's) no good, is it?] / كَرِهَ (To have a feeling of aversion or antipathy towards; not to like.)  [dislike (on social media, etc.)]",
 "良くなる": "حَسَّنَ (To make (something) better; to increase the value or productivity (of something)) / تَحَسَّنَ (To become better.)  [to improve]\nمثال: 明日になればきっと天候もよくなるだろう。\n→ The weather is bound to get better tomorrow.",
 "良く出来ました": "أَحْسَنْتَ, أَحْسَنْتِ (An exclamation of praise or endorsement of an achievement.)  [well done]\noft. stamped onto homework assignments etc. as the equiv. of a gold or silver star sticker",
 "良く考えたら": "فِعْلًا (In act or in fact; really; in truth; positively.)  [actually]",
 "良さ": "جَدَارَة (A claim to commendation or a reward.)  [merit]\nمثال: 彼は日本文化のよさを認めています。\n→ He appreciates Japanese culture.",
 "良し": "حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good]",
 "良しとする": "قِيمَة (The quality that renders something desirable or valuable; worth.)  [to value]",
 "良しなに": "كَمَا يَجِب, كَمَا يَنْبَغِي (In a proper manner, appropriately, suitably; correctly, justifiably)  [properly]",
