 "行き先": "وِجْهَة, وُجْهَة (The place set for the end of a journey or to which something is sent; place or p)  [destination]\nمثال: 彼は行き先の違う列車に乗るほど不注意ではない。\n→ He is not so careless as to take the wrong train. / [whereabouts]\nمثال: 行き先の住所はおわかりですか。\n→ Do you have an address? / مُسْتَقْبَل (The time ahead; those moments yet to be experienced.) / مُسْتَقْبَلِيّ, مُسْتَقْبَل (Having to do with or occurring in the future.)  [future]",
 "行き場": "وِجْهَة, وُجْهَة (The place set for the end of a journey or to which something is sent; place or p)  [destination]",
 "行き当たりばったり": "عَشْوَائِيّ (Occurring for no particular reason; haphazard, unpredictable.) / عَشْوَائِيّ (Involving an outcome which is impossible to predict, but which may be represente)  [random]\nمثال: 行き当たりばったりの仕事をするな。\n→ Don't leave everything to chance.",
 "行き当たる": "أَصَابَ (To manage to touch (a target) in the right place.) / ضَرْبَة (A blow; a punch; a striking against; the collision of one body against another; )  [to hit]\nمثال: 我々は暗闇の中で正しい道に行き当たった。\n→ We hit the right road in the dark.",
 "行き当る": "أَصَابَ (To manage to touch (a target) in the right place.) / ضَرْبَة (A blow; a punch; a striking against; the collision of one body against another; )  [to hit]\nمثال: 我々は暗闇の中で正しい道に行き当たった。\n→ We hit the right road in the dark.",
 "行き所": "وِجْهَة, وُجْهَة (The place set for the end of a journey or to which something is sent; place or p)  [destination]",
 "行き掛かり": "حَالَة, ظَرْف (Something which is related to, or in some way affects, a fact or event.)  [(by force of) circumstances]\nمثال: 行きがかり上しなけりゃならなかった。\n→ It just turned out that I had to do it.",
 "行き掛り": "حَالَة, ظَرْف (Something which is related to, or in some way affects, a fact or event.)  [(by force of) circumstances]\nمثال: 行きがかり上しなけりゃならなかった。\n→ It just turned out that I had to do it.",
 "行き損なう": "أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss (boat, plane, train, etc.)]",
 "行き摩り": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing]\nمثال: あの人は行きずりの人です。\n→ He is only a passing chance acquaintance. / [(place) that one happens to pass by] / مُؤَقَّت, سَريع الزوال (Passing or disappearing with time; transitory.)  [transient]",
 "行き摺り": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing]\nمثال: あの人は行きずりの人です。\n→ He is only a passing chance acquaintance. / [(place) that one happens to pass by] / مُؤَقَّت, سَريع الزوال (Passing or disappearing with time; transitory.)  [transient]",
 "行き方": "طَرِيق, سَبِيل (To do with a place or places.)  [way (of going)]\nمثال: 駅への行き方を教えてもらえますか。\n→ Could you tell me how to get to the station? / طَرِيق, سَبِيل (To do with a place or places.)  [way (of doing)]",
 "行き来": "[coming and going ; keeping in touch]\nمثال: 好きなように行き来していいですよ。\n→ You may come and go at will. / طَرِيق, طَرِيق عَامّ (A main public road, especially a multi-lane, high-speed thoroughfare.)  [highway]",
 "行き止まり": "طَرِيق مَسْدُود, طَرِيق غَيْر نَافِذ (A street or path or tunnel that goes nowhere or is blocked on one end.) / طَرِيق مَسْدُود (A position that offers no hope of change or progress.)  [dead end]\nمثال: その道は行き止まりだった。\n→ The road came to a dead end. / نِهَايَة, غَايَة (The most extreme point of an object, especially one that is longer than it is wi) / غَايَة (A purpose, goal, or aim.) / اِنْتَهَى, أَنْهَى (To finish, terminate.)  [end]",
 "行き渡る": "يسود (To be superior in strength, dominance, influence, or frequency; to have or gain )  [to prevail]\nمثال: この雑誌は広く行き渡っている。\n→ This magazine circulates widely.",
 "行き着く": "وَصَلَ (To reach; to get to a certain place.)  [to arrive (at one's destination)]\nمثال: 「時間通りに、教室にうまく行き着くことができる」と彼は思った。\n→ \"I can make it to my class on time,\" he thought. / [to come to a head ; to reach a conclusion]\nمثال: 労働側と経営側の意見不一致はストライキに行きつくかもしれない。\n→ The disagreement between the union and management could lead to a strike.",
 "行き脚": "زَخَم حَرَكَة (Of a body in motion: the tendency of a body to maintain its inertial motion; the) / زَخَم (The impetus, either of a body in motion, or of an idea or course of events; a mo)  [momentum (e.g. of a boat)]",
 "行き詰まり": "رَدْب (The state in which the player to move is not in check but has no legal moves, re) / طَرِيق مَسْدُود, مَأْزِق (Any situation that has no obvious possible movement, but involves no personal lo)  [stalemate]",
 "行き詰り": "رَدْب (The state in which the player to move is not in check but has no legal moves, re) / طَرِيق مَسْدُود, مَأْزِق (Any situation that has no obvious possible movement, but involves no personal lo)  [stalemate]",
 "行き足": "زَخَم حَرَكَة (Of a body in motion: the tendency of a body to maintain its inertial motion; the) / زَخَم (The impetus, either of a body in motion, or of an idea or course of events; a mo)  [momentum (e.g. of a boat)]",
 "行き路": "طَرِيق, مَسار (A course or way which is traveled or passed.)  [route (when going somewhere)]\nمثال: 少女は親切に博物館へ行く行き道を教えてくれた。\n→ The girl kindly told me the way to the museum.",
 "行き道": "طَرِيق, مَسار (A course or way which is traveled or passed.)  [route (when going somewhere)]\nمثال: 少女は親切に博物館へ行く行き道を教えてくれた。\n→ The girl kindly told me the way to the museum.",
 "行き違い": "[crossing without meeting (e.g. letters in the post, people on the road) ; going astray] / سُوء فَهْم (A mistake as to the meaning of something or a specific point of view; erroneous )  [misunderstanding]",
 "行き違いになる": "صَلِيب (A geometrical figure consisting of two straight lines or bars intersecting each ) / صَلِيب (A wooden post with a perpendicular beam attached and used (especially in the Rom) / صَلِيب (Alternative letter-case form of Cross (“the Crucifix, the cross on which Christ ) / عَبْر, خِلَال (The cross product of the previous vector and the following vector.) / عَبَرَ (To move relatively.)  [to cross (in the post)]\nمثال: 私たちの手紙は行き違いになった。\n→ Our letters crossed each other.",
 "行き違う": "صَلِيب (A geometrical figure consisting of two straight lines or bars intersecting each ) / صَلِيب (A wooden post with a perpendicular beam attached and used (especially in the Rom) / صَلِيب (Alternative letter-case form of Cross (“the Crucifix, the cross on which Christ ) / عَبْر, خِلَال (The cross product of the previous vector and the following vector.) / عَبَرَ (To move relatively.)  [to cross (each other)] / صَلِيب (A geometrical figure consisting of two straight lines or bars intersecting each ) / صَلِيب (A wooden post with a perpendicular beam attached and used (especially in the Rom) / صَلِيب (Alternative letter-case form of Cross (“the Crucifix, the cross on which Christ ) / عَبْر, خِلَال (The cross product of the previous vector and the following vector.) / عَبَرَ (To move relatively.)  [to cross (of letters in the mail)] / تَصَادُم (A skirmish, a hostile encounter.) / يتصادم (To come into violent conflict.)  [to clash]",
 "行く": "ذَهَبَ, رَاحَ (To move, either physically or in an abstract sense:) / ذَهَبَ, زَالَ (To pass, to be used up:) / غُو (A strategic board game, originally from China and today also popular in Japan an)  [to go]\nمثال: お母さん、泳ぎに行ってもいい？\n→ Can I go swimming, Mother? / [to move through ; to travel across]\nمثال: 探検家が山中の道なき道を行った。\n→ The explorer pushed his way through the trackless mountain region. / ذَهَبَ, رَاحَ (To move, either physically or in an abstract sense:) / ذَهَبَ, زَالَ (To pass, to be used up:) / غُو (A strategic board game, originally from China and today also popular in Japan an)  [to go (well, badly, etc.)]\nمثال: あなたのおかげで仕事がうまく行きました。\n→ Thanks to you, the job went well. / فَعَلَ, عَمِلَ (To perform; to execute.) / دُو, دُو (A syllable used in solfège to represent the first and eighth tonic of a major sc)  [to do (in a particular way)]\noft. as で〜",
 "行く先": "وِجْهَة, وُجْهَة (The place set for the end of a journey or to which something is sent; place or p)  [destination] / [whereabouts] / مُسْتَقْبَل (The time ahead; those moments yet to be experienced.) / مُسْتَقْبَلِيّ, مُسْتَقْبَل (Having to do with or occurring in the future.)  [future]",
