 "行って来": "إِلَى اللِّقَاء (short for goodbye — see also goodbye) / مَعَ السَّلَامَة (short for goodbye — see also goodbye) / سَلَام (short for goodbye — see also goodbye)  [bye]",
 "行って来い": "تَذَبذُب, تَقَلُّب (A wavering; unsteadiness.)  [fluctuation (e.g. in a market)]",
 "行って来ます": "إِلَى اللِّقَاء, أَرَاكَ لَاحِقًا (A phrase used at parting, and not necessarily implying that the person being add)  [see you later]\noften has a response of いってらっしゃい\nمثال: 一時間したら行ってきます。\n→ I'm going out in an hour.",
 "行って来る": "إِلَى اللِّقَاء, أَرَاكَ لَاحِقًا (A phrase used at parting, and not necessarily implying that the person being add)  [see you later] / ذَهَبَ, رَاحَ (To move, either physically or in an abstract sense:) / ذَهَبَ, زَالَ (To pass, to be used up:) / غُو (A strategic board game, originally from China and today also popular in Japan an)  [to go (and then come back)]\nمثال: ちょっと郵便局へいってくる。\n→ I'm just going to drop by the post office.",
 "行ない": "مَأْثُرَة (A brave or noteworthy action; a feat or exploit.)  [deed]\nمثال: 彼は勇気ある行いをした。\n→ He did a courageous act. / سُلُوك, تَصَرُّف (The way or manner a living creature behaves or acts generally.)  [behavior]\nمثال: そのような行ないはいかにもメグらしい。\n→ Such behavior is just like Meg. / زُهْد (The principles and practices of an ascetic; extreme self-denial and austerity.)  [asceticism]",
 "行なう": "أَدَّى (To do (something); to execute.)  [to perform]\nمثال: 自分の責任において何でも行いなさい。\n→ Do everything at your own risk.",
 "行なわれる": "حَدَثَ, جَرَى (To happen or to occur.)  [to take place]\nمثال: そのパーティーはいつ行われますか。\n→ When will the party take place?",
 "行われる": "حَدَثَ, جَرَى (To happen or to occur.)  [to take place]\nمثال: そのパーティーはいつ行われますか。\n→ When will the party take place?",
 "行事": "وَاقِعَة, حَادِثَة (An occurrence; something that happens.)  [event]\nمثال: メグは学校のいろいろな行事に参加する。\n→ Meg attends many school affairs.",
 "行交い": "مُرُور (pedestrians or vehicles on roads or on the air)  [traffic]",
 "行人": "مَارّ, مَارَّة (A person who is passing by (that is, walking past).)  [passer-by]",
 "行付け": "عَادِيّ (Having a constant pattern; showing evenness of form or appearance.) / مُنْتَظِمٌ (Both equilateral and equiangular; having all sides of the same length, and all () / عَادِيّ (Having the expected characteristics or appearances; normal, ordinary, standard.)  [regular]\nمثال: 近所に行きつけの店があるから、今日はそこでランチを食べよう。\n→ I'm a regular at a restaurant in this neighborhood. Let's have lunch there today.",
 "行付ける": "مُتَكَرِّر (Done or occurring often; common.) / اِرْتَادَ (To visit often.)  [to frequent]",
 "行使": "اِسْتِعْمَال, اِسْتِخْدَام (The act of using.) / اِسْتَعْمَلَ, اِسْتَخْدَمَ (To utilize or employ.)  [use]\nمثال: ニクソンはウォーターゲート事件に関し、黙秘権を行使して無視しようとしたが、結局明るみにでた。\n→ Nixon tried to stonewall through Watergate by ignoring it, but it didn't work.",
