 "行儀作法": "ذَوْق, آدَاب (The manners or decent behaviour to be observed in social or professional life; c)  [etiquette]\nمثال: 私の母は行儀作法にやかましい。\n→ My mother is strict about manners.",
 "行儀悪い": "غَيْر مُطِيع, شَقِيّ (Mischievous; tending to misbehave or act badly (especially of a child).)  [naughty]",
 "行先": "وِجْهَة, وُجْهَة (The place set for the end of a journey or to which something is sent; place or p)  [destination]\nمثال: 彼は行き先の違う列車に乗るほど不注意ではない。\n→ He is not so careless as to take the wrong train. / [whereabouts]\nمثال: 行き先の住所はおわかりですか。\n→ Do you have an address? / مُسْتَقْبَل (The time ahead; those moments yet to be experienced.) / مُسْتَقْبَلِيّ, مُسْتَقْبَل (Having to do with or occurring in the future.)  [future]",
 "行列": "خَطّ (The wire connecting one telegraphic station with another, a telephone or interne)  [line]\nمثال: 子どもたちがサーカスの行列を追いかけた。\n→ The children chased after the circus parade. / مَصْفُوفَة (A rectangular arrangement of numbers or terms having various uses such as transf)  [matrix]",
 "行列式": "مُحَدِّد (A determining factor; an element that determines the nature of something.) / مُحَدِّد (A scalar that encodes certain characteristics of a given transformation matrix; )  [determinant]\nمثال: 数学。行列式のところが宿題になってるんだけど・・・どうも僕にはついていけなくて・・・。\n→ Maths. Homework's about derivatives, but I really can't seem to cope with it.",
 "行動": "عَمَل (Something done, often so as to accomplish a purpose.)  [action]\nمثال: 彼は友人の行動に憤慨した。\n→ He resented his friend's action.",
 "行動に移る": "نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [to start]",
 "行動をとる": "عَمَل (Something done, a deed.) / قَانُون ((In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become la) / مَثَّلَ (To perform a theatrical role.) / تَصَرَّفَ (To behave in a certain manner for an indefinite length of time.)  [to act]",
 "行動を取る": "عَمَل (Something done, a deed.) / قَانُون ((In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become la) / مَثَّلَ (To perform a theatrical role.) / تَصَرَّفَ (To behave in a certain manner for an indefinite length of time.)  [to act]",
 "行動主義": "[behaviorism ; behaviourism] / نَشَاطِيَّة (The practice of using action to achieve a result, such as political demonstratio)  [activism]",
 "行動力": "طَاقَة (The impetus behind all motion and all activity.) / طَاقَة (The capacity to do work.) / طَاقَة (A quantity that denotes the ability to do work and is measured in a unit dimensi)  [energy]\nمثال: 見かけ通り彼女は行動力がある。\n→ She is as active as she looks.",
