 "見張り所": "نَاطُور (A person on watch for approaching enemy, police, danger, etc.)  [lookout]",
 "見張り番": "حَارِس (A person who, or thing that, protects or watches over something.) / حَرَسَ (To protect from danger; to secure against surprise, attack, or injury; to keep i)  [guard]",
 "見張る": "حا َسـِب (To be vigilant and aware often as an imperative to alert a person to danger.)  [to look out]\nمثال: ビキニスタイルの美少女は浜辺では目を見張らすものだった。\n→ The pretty girl in the bikini was an eye-opener on the beach. / [to open (one's eyes) wide]",
