 "言い返す": "أَجَابَ, رَدَّ (To give a written or spoken response, especially to a question, request, accusat) / إِجَابَة, جَوَاب (A written or spoken response; part of a conversation.)  [to reply]\nمثال: ベスは言い返しましたが、お母さんは彼女にものすごく太りすぎていると注意しました。\n→ Beth protested, but her mother reminded her that she was incredibly fat. / كَرَّرَ, أَعَادَ (To do or say again (and again).)  [to repeat (what one has said)]",
 "言い逃がれ": "عَذَرَ (To forgive; to pardon; to overlook.) / اِعْتَذَرَ (To allow to leave, or release from any obligation.) / عُذْر (An explanation designed to avoid or alleviate guilt or negative judgment; a plea)  [excuse]\nمثال: 忙しいからその仕事ができないというのは単なる言い逃れじゃないか。\n→ Saying you can't do the job because you're too busy is just a cop out.",
 "言い逃れ": "عَذَرَ (To forgive; to pardon; to overlook.) / اِعْتَذَرَ (To allow to leave, or release from any obligation.) / عُذْر (An explanation designed to avoid or alleviate guilt or negative judgment; a plea)  [excuse]\nمثال: 忙しいからその仕事ができないというのは単なる言い逃れじゃないか。\n→ Saying you can't do the job because you're too busy is just a cop out.",
 "言い過ぎ": "مُبَالَغَة (The act of exaggerating; the act of doing or representing in an excessive manner)  [exaggeration]\nمثال: 彼が天才であるというのは言い過ぎではない。\n→ It is not too much to say that he is a genius.",
 "言い過ぎる": "بَالَغَ (To overstate, to describe more than the fact.)  [to exaggerate]\nمثال: ちょっときつく言い過ぎたかな、とずっと思っています。\n→ I've been thinking that I may have been too critical.",
 "言い過ごす": "بَالَغَ (To overstate, to describe more than the fact.)  [to exaggerate]",
 "言い開き": "عَذَرَ (To forgive; to pardon; to overlook.) / اِعْتَذَرَ (To allow to leave, or release from any obligation.) / عُذْر (An explanation designed to avoid or alleviate guilt or negative judgment; a plea)  [excuse]",
