 "言う": "قَالَ, قال (To pronounce.) / يَتْلُو (To recite.) / قَالَ, قَالَ (To tell, either verbally or in writing.)  [to say]\nمثال: 「みんなひと休みしようぜ」とジョンは言った。\n→ John said, \"Hey guys, let's take a break.\" / اِسْم, أَسْمَاء (Any nounal word or phrase which indicates a particular person, place, class, or ) / اِشْتِهَار (A reputation.) / سَمَّى, سمى (To give a name to.) / اِخْتَارَ (To mention, specify.) / عَيَّنَ (To publicly implicate by name.) / عَيَّنَ, نَصَبَ (To designate for a role.)  [to name]\nمثال: この動物は日本語で何と言いますか。\n→ What do you call this animal in Japanese? / ذَهَبَ, رَاحَ (To move, either physically or in an abstract sense:) / ذَهَبَ, زَالَ (To pass, to be used up:) / غُو (A strategic board game, originally from China and today also popular in Japan an)  [to go (e.g. \"the alarm went ping\")]",
 "言うことを聞く": "[to do what one is told to (esp. of a child) ; to take someone's advice]\nمثال: その少年は両親の言うことを聞く。\n→ The boy is obedient to his parents. / أَطَاعَ (To do as ordered by (a person, institution etc), to act according to the bidding)  [to obey (one)]\noft. in the negative",
