 "言わぬは言うに優る": "إِنْ كَانَ الْكَلَامُ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ فَالسُّكُوتُ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ (Not saying anything is often better than speaking too much or saying something i)  [speech is silver, silence is golden]",
